 "post": {
  "title": "Same Speech, Lower Voice, More Votes #shorts",
  "description": "Priya is pitching to lead her team, but every sentence ends like a question. In 2012 Casey Klofstad, Rindy Anderson and Susan Peters (\"Sounds like a winner: voice pitch influences perception of leadership capacity in both men and women\", Proceedings of the Royal Society B) recorded men and women saying \"I urge you to vote for me this November\", then made higher- and lower-pitched versions of each voice. Both men and women listeners picked the lower-pitched candidates, for male and female voices, and lower voices were often rated stronger and more competent. Caveat: a lab test with edited recordings, not a real election. #psychology #shorts #leadership #publicspeaking",
